        "title": "Limit sign-up attempts per email address",
        "given": "the same email address is used in multiple sign-up attempts",
        "when": "attempts exceed threshold within time window",
        "then": "block further sign-ups for that email and require additional verification like CAPTCHA"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "InformationDisclosure",
      "title": "Referral codes may be enumerable, revealing which users exist",
      "scenario": "If referral codes are sequential, short, or follow predictable patterns (user123, abc001), an attacker can enumerate them to discover which codes are valid, thereby learning which users have accounts. This information could be used for targeted phishing, social engineering, or competitive intelligence gathering.",
