      "cwe": ["CWE-330"],
      "plainLanguage": "If referral codes are easy to guess, attackers could figure out which users have accounts",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Generate cryptographically random referral codes",
        "given": "a new user account is created",
        "when": "referral code is generated",
        "then": "use cryptographically secure random values with sufficient entropy (at least 128 bits) to prevent enumeration attacks"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "Tampering",
      "title": "Race condition in credit allocation could duplicate rewards",
      "scenario": "If multiple users sign up simultaneously using the same referral code, and the credit allocation system doesn't use proper locking or atomic operations, the referrer could receive credits multiple times for what should be a single transaction. An attacker who discovers this timing window could exploit it deliberately with parallel requests to gain extra credits.",
